Z||000025||DaRkLoRD||12-13-2000||05:48 PM||||When I'm done with my Fiero, it's gonna be extremely modified.. no stickers or huge exhaust tips though... I might put a windshield banner across the top, but it'd be very small and unobtrusive.. as for the exhaust, I'm going for 4 2.5" chrome tips, attached to a flowmaster.. that's more than enough for a 2.8 IMHO.<P>point is, there's a difference between real mods and "sticker mods"..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000026||Slammed Fiero||12-14-2000||02:50 PM||||Modifying your car is all about individuality... I don't think it's an age thing at all. Ok cars with 9000 decals all over them are cheezy , but the right mods tastefully done  personalize a car. Perhaps an age thing , I wonder when it ends?? Lets see my dad at 60 years old drives numerous modified cars...we don't own one vehicle that hasn't had something done to it to enhance looks or performance..or both. <P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...||||reg||1
Z||000027||Phil||12-14-2000||04:42 PM||||I would start with a brake upgrade and new shocks and struts, that way you will have a good solid foundation to build on.||||reg||1
Z||000028||RiceCooker||12-14-2000||05:15 PM||||It's a tough call cause there's so much to do with so little time and money. (if that's your case)<BR>On one hand, you definitley want your car to look good but you want the performance to back it up. If some guy really likes your car, pulls you over and asks what she does in the 1/4 mile, you don't want to have to say..."Oh, about high 16's"<BR>On the other hand, there's no better feeling than being a sleeper. That is, some punk a$$ kid pulls up in his mommy's neon and wants to race your stock looking fiero so you spank him! <BR>I guess i don't have a defintive answer, just more incoherent babble.<P>bfhsbdfbsfwfuiwfuyww, <BR>Todd<P>P.S. I'd like to buy a vowel||||reg||1
Z||000029||Monkeyman||12-14-2000||05:18 PM||||Ditto what Phil said.  And if you're into sound, try upgrading the stereo next.  Body mods are great (I have several on my wish list), but they tend to get expensive once you include body prep, paint, etc into the  price tag.  Try some larger wheels and wider tires, lowering springs, etc.<P>Here's what I'm planning on doing to my new (soon) GT (yes, another '85, of course):  IRM Integrated Rockers, whale tail, Toms scoop, change the vented engine covers for solid '84 style ones, lowered, 16" rims, etc, etc.<P>Money's gotten fairly tight lately due to some unfortunate happenings, but I <I>will</I> have a killer car once I'm finished.||||reg||1
